{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Young I (Thomas Young, 1800)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"youngI"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Four fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, and A→E — are each narrowed by 3\/16 of the syntonic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comma, equal to (3\/2)·(80\/81)^(3\/16) ≈ 697.923 cents. Four more fifths — E→B,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"B→F♯, B♭→F, and F→C — are each narrowed by (¼ PC − 3\/16 SC) ≈ 1.833 cents,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equal to (3\/2)·(81\/80)^(3\/16)·(2¹⁹\/3¹²)^(−1\/4) ≈ 700.122 cents. The remaining","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"four fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Published in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" 90 (1800).","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/youngi"]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"key